<!-- ll-bracket demo — mirrors the upstream docs page (#/components/bracket).
     The grouping-list example swaps the (not yet ported) callout for a plain
     hand note; revisit when ll-callout lands. -->
<view class="demo">
  <ll-page-title underline="highlight" seed="bracket" custom-style="margin-bottom:16rpx;">Bracket</ll-page-title>
  <view class="sec-desc">A hand-drawn bracket down one side of a stretch of content — square, curly or round — grouping it like a margin note.</view>

  <view class="sec sec--grid">
    <view class="sec-h2">Preview</view>
    <view class="sub-h3">Default</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">A square bracket down the start side of two paragraphs.</view>
    <view class="stack">
      <ll-bracket custom-style="max-width:768rpx">
        <view class="para">These two paragraphs are one idea, and the bracket says so.</view>
        <view class="para" style="margin-top:16rpx">You could nod and keep reading, or you could underline them and come back next week.</view>
      </ll-bracket>
    </view>
  </view>

  <view class="sec sec--grid">
    <view class="sec-h2">Examples</view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Kinds and sides</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">Square, curly and round; on the start side and the end side; in ink, blue and red.</view>
    <view class="grid2">
      <ll-bracket kind="square" custom-style="width:384rpx">
        <view class="para">Square: for quoting a stretch of a page.</view>
      </ll-bracket>
      <ll-bracket kind="curly" tone="blue" side="end" custom-style="width:384rpx">
        <view class="para">Curly: for lumping things together, from the end side.</view>
      </ll-bracket>
      <ll-bracket kind="round" tone="red" custom-style="width:384rpx">
        <view class="para">Round: for an aside.</view>
      </ll-bracket>
      <ll-bracket kind="square" weight="brush" tone="ink" side="end" custom-style="width:384rpx">
        <view class="para">A brush pen makes it a statement.</view>
      </ll-bracket>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Grouping list items</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">A curly brace across three items with a note on the other side: the list is still a list.</view>
    <view class="stack">
      <view class="group-row">
        <ll-bracket kind="curly" side="end" tone="blue" custom-style="padding-right:64rpx">
          <view class="list">
            <view>Flour</view>
            <view>Butter</view>
            <view>Sugar</view>
          </view>
        </ll-bracket>
        <view class="note">the base</view>
      </view>
    </view>
  </view>
</view>
